   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🇮🇳 Hindi Corpus Collection & Tokenizer Training (Model H)\n",
    "**Course**: Language Models and Agents (CL3-410) — Monsoon 2026  \n",
    "**Author**: 24KaratAu  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Pipeline Overview:\n",
    "1. **Manual Collection (≥20%)**: Full Hindi Wikipedia (`hiwiki`) and Wikisource (`hiwikisource`) XML bz2 dumps extracted, cleaned, and deduplicated in-house.\n",
    "2. **Automated Collection (≤80%)**: Streamed human-verified records from AI4Bharat Sangraha Verified via PyArrow micro-batching.\n",
    "3. **Exact Deduplication**: 64-bit integer SHA-256 hash sets with manual priority registration to prevent overlap.\n",
    "4. **Split Generation**: Deterministic 90/5/5 document-level train/validation/test partitions.\n",
    "5. **Tokenizer Training**: SentencePiece Byte-Pair Encoding (BPE) trained from scratch with **8,000 (8k)** subword vocabulary (TA recommended 5k–10k), `byte_fallback=True` (0.00% UNK), and Devanagari script isolation.\n",
    "6. **Intrinsic Evaluation**: Benchmark metrics grounded in *Dwivedi & Gopalan (ACL 2026)*."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## 0. Environment Setup & Crash-Resilient Resume"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "DRIVE_BASE = '/content/drive/MyDrive/24KaratAu/hindi'\n",
    "for d in ['raw/wiki_dump', 'cleaned/manual', 'cleaned/automated_nonweb',\n",
    "          'cleaned/automated_web', 'splits', 'tokenizer']:\n",
    "    os.makedirs(f'{DRIVE_BASE}/{d}', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print('✅ Drive directories verified at:', DRIVE_BASE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q pandas pyarrow sentencepiece trafilatura requests\n",
    "print('✅ Dependencies installed')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json, hashlib, re, random, bz2, os, gc, sys, shutil, math, collections\n",
    "import urllib.request\n",
    "import pyarrow.parquet as pq\n",
    "import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "\n",
    "LANGUAGE = 'hindi'\n",
    "MIN_CHARS = 100\n",
    "MIN_DEV_RATIO = 0.50\n",
    "SHARD_SIZE = 5000\n",
    "\n",
    "# Token calculation constants\n",
    "CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 6\n",
    "MANUAL_TOKEN_TARGET = 100_000_000  # >= 20% manual floor (100M tokens)\n",
    "TOTAL_TOKEN_TARGET  = 500_000_000  # ~500M total target\n",
    "AUTO_TOKEN_TARGET   = 400_000_000  # <= 80% automated share (400M tokens)\n",
    "AUTO_CHAR_TARGET    = AUTO_TOKEN_TARGET * CHARS_PER_TOKEN\n",
    "\n",
    "MANUAL_DIR = f'{DRIVE_BASE}/cleaned/manual'\n",
    "NONWEB_DIR = f'{DRIVE_BASE}/cleaned/automated_nonweb'\n",
    "WEB_DIR    = f'{DRIVE_BASE}/cleaned/automated_web'\n",
    "SPLITS_DIR = f'{DRIVE_BASE}/splits'\n",
    "TOKENIZER_DIR = f'{DRIVE_BASE}/tokenizer'\n",
    "\n",
    "def devanagari_ratio(text):\n",
    "    if not text: return 0.0\n",
    "    return sum(1 for c in text if '\\u0900' <= c <= '\\u097F') / len(text)\n",
    "\n",
    "def clean_web_text(text):\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'https?://\\S+', '', text)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'\\S+@\\S+\\.\\S+', '', text)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'&[a-zA-Z]+;', ' ', text)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'&#\\d+;', ' ', text)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'[ \\t]+', ' ', text)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'\\n{3,}', '\\n\\n', text)\n",
    "    return text.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "def text_hash_int(text):\n",
    "    \"\"\"64-bit integer hash to reduce deduplication RAM usage by 75%.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return int(hashlib.sha256(text.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()[:16], 16)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── RESUME EXISTING RUN ──\n",
    "all_hashes = set()\n",
    "existing_manual_chars = 0\n",
    "existing_auto_chars = 0\n",
    "existing_docs = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "for d in [MANUAL_DIR, NONWEB_DIR, WEB_DIR]:\n",
    "    for sf in sorted(Path(d).glob('*.jsonl')):\n",
    "        with open(sf, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "            for line in f:\n",
    "                if not line.strip(): continue\n",
    "                try:\n",
    "                    doc = json.loads(line)\n",
    "                    h = doc.get('text_sha256', '')\n",
    "                    if h:\n",
    "                        all_hashes.add(int(h[:16], 16) if len(h) > 16 else int(h, 16))\n",
    "                    existing_docs += 1\n",
    "                    c = doc.get('clean_text_characters', len(doc.get('text', '')))\n",
    "                    if doc.get('collection_type') == 'manual':\n",
    "                        existing_manual_chars += c\n",
    "                    else:\n",
    "                        existing_auto_chars += c\n",
    "                except: pass\n",
    "\n",
    "if existing_docs > 0:\n",
    "    print(f'🔄 RESUMING: {existing_docs:,} docs | Manual: ~{existing_manual_chars//CHARS_PER_TOKEN:,} tokens | Auto: ~{existing_auto_chars//CHARS_PER_TOKEN:,} tokens')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('📦 Fresh pipeline initialized')\n",
    "print(f'✅ Hash set ready ({len(all_hashes):,} hashes in memory)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 1: Manual Collection (Wikipedia & Wikisource Dumps)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Manual Priority Rule**: Manual dumps are parsed and registered into `all_hashes` FIRST. This guarantees that automated web crawls cannot overwrite or collide with manual articles."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "WIKI_DUMP = '/content/hiwiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2'\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(WIKI_DUMP):\n",
    "    print('📥 Downloading Hindi Wikipedia XML dump (~600MB)...')\n",
    "    !wget -q --show-progress -O {WIKI_DUMP} \\\n",
    "        'https://dumps.wikimedia.org/hiwiki/latest/hiwiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2'\n",
    "print(f'✅ Hindi Wikipedia dump ready: {os.path.getsize(WIKI_DUMP)/(1024*1024):.1f} MB')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cleaning regex patterns\n",
    "WIKI_MARKUP = [\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\{\\{[^}]*\\}\\}'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[\\[Category:[^\\]]*\\]\\]'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[\\[श्रेणी:[^\\]]*\\]\\]'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[\\[वर्ग:[^\\]]*\\]\\]'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[\\[[^|\\]]*\\|([^\\]]*)\\]\\]'), r'\\1'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\]'), r'\\1'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[https?://[^\\s\\]]*\\s*([^\\]]*)\\]'), r'\\1'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[https?://[^\\]]*\\]'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r\"'{2,5}\"), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'<ref[^>]*>.*?</ref>', re.DOTALL), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'<ref[^/>]*/>'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'<[^>]+>'), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'&[a-zA-Z]+;'), ' '),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'\\[\\d+\\]'), ''),\n",
    "]\n",
    "TABLE_PAT = [\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^\\s*\\{\\|.*$', re.MULTILINE), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^\\s*\\|\\}.*$', re.MULTILINE), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^\\s*\\|-.*$', re.MULTILINE), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^\\s*!.*$', re.MULTILINE), ''),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^\\|.*$', re.MULTILINE), ''),\n",
    "]\n",
    "SKIP_SEC = {'सन्दर्भ', 'संदर्भ', 'बाहरी कड़ियाँ', 'बाहरी कड़ी', 'श्रेणी',\n",
    "            'इन्हें भी देखें', 'यह भी देखें', 'स्रोत', 'टिप्पणी', 'नोट',\n",
    "            'references', 'external links', 'see also', 'notes'}\n",
    "\n",
    "def clean_wiki(text):\n",
    "    for p, r in TABLE_PAT: text = p.sub(r, text)\n",
    "    for p, r in WIKI_MARKUP: text = p.sub(r, text)\n",
    "    lines, result, skip = text.split('\\n'), [], False\n",
    "    for line in lines:\n",
    "        s = line.strip().lower()\n",
    "        if s in SKIP_SEC: skip = True; continue\n",
    "        if re.match(r'^={2,}.*={2,}$', s): skip = False\n",
    "        if not skip: result.append(line)\n",
    "    text = '\\n'.join(result)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'[ \\t]+', ' ', text)\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'\\n{3,}', '\\n\\n', text)\n",
    "    return text.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "with bz2.open(WIKI_DUMP, 'rt', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "    header = f.read(5000)\n",
    "    ns_match = re.search(r'xmlns=\"(http://www\\.mediawiki\\.org/xml/export-[^\"]+)\"', header)\n",
    "    NS = '{' + ns_match.group(1) + '}' if ns_match else ''\n",
    "print(f'✅ XML namespace detected: {NS or \"default\"}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "man_docs = []\n",
    "man_chars = existing_manual_chars\n",
    "man_count = 0\n",
    "man_shard = len(list(Path(MANUAL_DIR).glob('*.jsonl')))\n",
    "seen, skipped_dup, rejected = 0, 0, 0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Parsing Hindi Wikipedia dump with zero-RAM root.clear() streaming...')\n",
    "\n",
    "with bz2.open(WIKI_DUMP, 'rt', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "    context = ET.iterparse(f, events=('start', 'end'))\n",
    "    context = iter(context)\n",
    "    event, root = next(context)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for event, elem in context:\n",
    "        tag = elem.tag.split('}')[-1] if '}' in elem.tag else elem.tag\n",
    "        if event != 'end' or tag != 'page': continue\n",
    "        \n",
    "        ns_el = elem.find(f'{NS}ns') if NS else elem.find('ns')\n",
    "        if ns_el is None or ns_el.text != '0':\n",
    "            elem.clear(); root.clear(); continue\n",
    "        redirect = elem.find(f'{NS}redirect') if NS else elem.find('redirect')\n",
    "        if redirect is not None:\n",
    "            elem.clear(); root.clear(); continue\n",
    "            \n",
    "        title_el = elem.find(f'{NS}title') if NS else elem.find('title')\n",
    "        id_el = elem.find(f'{NS}id') if NS else elem.find('id')\n",
    "        title = title_el.text if title_el is not None else ''\n",
    "        pid = id_el.text if id_el is not None else ''\n",
    "        rev = elem.find(f'{NS}revision') if NS else elem.find('revision')\n",
    "        raw = ''\n",
    "        if rev is not None:\n",
    "            te = rev.find(f'{NS}text') if NS else rev.find('text')\n",
    "            if te is not None and te.text: raw = te.text\n",
    "            \n",
    "        elem.clear(); root.clear()  # Critical memory leak fix\n",
    "        if not raw.strip(): continue\n",
    "        seen += 1\n",
    "        cleaned = clean_wiki(raw)\n",
    "        if len(cleaned) < MIN_CHARS or devanagari_ratio(cleaned) < MIN_DEV_RATIO:\n",
    "            rejected += 1; continue\n",
    "            \n",
    "        hi = text_hash_int(cleaned)\n",
    "        if hi in all_hashes: skipped_dup += 1; continue\n",
    "        all_hashes.add(hi)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        man_docs.append({\n",
    "            'doc_id': f'{pid}_{title}',\n",
    "            'title': title, 'wiki_page_id': pid,\n",
    "            'source': 'Hindi Wikipedia Dump', 'source_type': 'wikipedia_dump',\n",
    "            'collection_type': 'manual', 'language': LANGUAGE,\n",
    "            'text': cleaned, 'clean_text_characters': len(cleaned),\n",
    "            'devanagari_ratio': round(devanagari_ratio(cleaned), 4),\n",
    "            'text_sha256': f'{hi:x}',\n",
    "        })\n",
    "        man_chars += len(cleaned); man_count += 1\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if len(man_docs) >= SHARD_SIZE:\n",
    "            sf = f'{MANUAL_DIR}/wiki_shard_{man_shard:04d}.jsonl'\n",
    "            with open(sf, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as out:\n",
    "                for d in man_docs: out.write(json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n",
    "            print(f'  ✅ Saved {Path(sf).name} ({len(man_docs):,} docs)')\n",
    "            man_docs = []; man_shard += 1; gc.collect()\n",
    "            \n",
    "        if seen % 20000 == 0:\n",
    "            print(f'  [Progress] Seen: {seen:,} | Accepted: {man_count:,} | Chars: {man_chars:,}')\n",
    "\n",
    "if man_docs:\n",
    "    sf = f'{MANUAL_DIR}/wiki_shard_{man_shard:04d}.jsonl'\n",
    "    with open(sf, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as out:\n",
    "        for d in man_docs: out.write(json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n",
    "    print(f'  ✅ Final shard saved: {Path(sf).name} ({len(man_docs):,} docs)')\n",
    "    man_docs = []; gc.collect()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 65)\n",
    "print(f'MANUAL STEP 1 COMPLETE: {man_count:,} articles, {man_chars:,} clean chars (~{man_chars//CHARS_PER_TOKEN:,} tokens)')\n",
    "print('=' * 65)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 2: Sangraha Verified Automated Collection\n",
    "\n",
    "Streams 340MB parquet chunks from AI4Bharat Sangraha Verified in 5,000-row micro-batches. Automatically dedups against Step 1 manual hashes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "auto_chars_so_far = existing_auto_chars\n",
    "nonweb_docs = []\n",
    "nonweb_shard_idx = len(list(Path(NONWEB_DIR).glob('*.jsonl')))\n",
    "nonweb_total_chars = 0\n",
    "nonweb_total_docs = 0\n",
    "type_counts = Counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "def flush_nonweb():\n",
    "    global nonweb_docs, nonweb_shard_idx\n",
    "    if not nonweb_docs: return\n",
    "    sf = f'{NONWEB_DIR}/nonweb_shard_{nonweb_shard_idx:04d}.jsonl'\n",
    "    with open(sf, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "        for d in nonweb_docs:\n",
    "            f.write(json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n",
    "    print(f'  ✅ Saved shard to Drive: {Path(sf).name} ({len(nonweb_docs):,} docs)')\n",
    "    nonweb_docs = []\n",
    "    nonweb_shard_idx += 1\n",
    "    gc.collect()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Querying Hugging Face API for Sangraha verified Hindi shards...')\n",
    "api_url = 'https://huggingface.co/api/datasets/ai4bharat/sangraha'\n",
    "req = urllib.request.Request(api_url, headers={'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0'})\n",
    "with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:\n",
    "    repo_data = json.loads(resp.read().decode())\n",
    "    all_files = [f.get('rfilename') for f in repo_data.get('siblings', [])]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter for 340MB files data-1.parquet onwards\n",
    "hin_files = sorted([f for f in all_files if f.startswith('verified/hin/') and f.endswith('.parquet') and 'data-0.parquet' not in f])\n",
    "print(f'✅ Found {len(hin_files)} parquet shards')\n",
    "print(f'Target: {AUTO_CHAR_TARGET:,} auto chars (~{AUTO_TOKEN_TARGET//1_000_000}M tokens)\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "if auto_chars_so_far >= AUTO_CHAR_TARGET:\n",
    "    print('✅ Already reached automated target! Skipping.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    for idx, rel_path in enumerate(hin_files):\n",
    "        if auto_chars_so_far >= AUTO_CHAR_TARGET:\n",
    "            print('🎯 HIT AUTOMATED TARGET! Stopping stream.')\n",
    "            break\n",
    "            \n",
    "        file_name = Path(rel_path).name\n",
    "        temp_local = f'/content/{file_name}'\n",
    "        dl_url = f'https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/sangraha/resolve/main/{rel_path}'\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(f'📥 [{idx+1}/{len(hin_files)}] Downloading {file_name} (~340MB)...')\n",
    "        urllib.request.urlretrieve(dl_url, temp_local)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        pf = pq.ParquetFile(temp_local)\n",
    "        print(f'   Streaming {pf.metadata.num_rows:,} records in 5,000-row batches...')\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for batch in pf.iter_batches(batch_size=5000, columns=['text', 'type']):\n",
    "            batch_df = batch.to_pandas()\n",
    "            for row in batch_df.itertuples():\n",
    "                doc_type = str(getattr(row, 'type', '')).strip().lower()\n",
    "                type_counts[doc_type] += 1\n",
    "                \n",
    "                text = str(getattr(row, 'text', ''))\n",
    "                if not text or text == 'nan': continue\n",
    "                cleaned = clean_web_text(text)\n",
    "                if len(cleaned) < MIN_CHARS or devanagari_ratio(cleaned) < MIN_DEV_RATIO: continue\n",
    "                \n",
    "                hi = text_hash_int(cleaned)\n",
    "                if hi in all_hashes: continue\n",
    "                all_hashes.add(hi)\n",
    "                \n",
    "                nonweb_docs.append({\n",
    "                    'doc_id': f'{hi:x}',\n",
    "                    'source': 'sangraha', 'source_type': f'hf_sangraha_{doc_type}',\n",
    "                    'collection_type': 'automated', 'language': LANGUAGE,\n",
    "                    'text': cleaned, 'clean_text_characters': len(cleaned),\n",
    "                    'devanagari_ratio': round(devanagari_ratio(cleaned), 4),\n",
    "                    'text_sha256': f'{hi:x}', 'sangraha_type': doc_type,\n",
    "                })\n",
    "                nonweb_total_chars += len(cleaned)\n",
    "                nonweb_total_docs += 1\n",
    "                auto_chars_so_far += len(cleaned)\n",
    "                \n",
    "                if len(nonweb_docs) >= SHARD_SIZE: flush_nonweb()\n",
    "                if auto_chars_so_far >= AUTO_CHAR_TARGET: break\n",
    "            del batch_df\n",
    "            gc.collect()\n",
    "            if auto_chars_so_far >= AUTO_CHAR_TARGET: break\n",
    "            \n",
    "        if os.path.exists(temp_local):\n",
    "            os.remove(temp_local)\n",
    "        gc.collect()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        pct = auto_chars_so_far / AUTO_CHAR_TARGET * 100\n",
    "        print(f'   ✅ {file_name} processed | Docs: {nonweb_total_docs:,} | Progress: {pct:.1f}%\\n')\n",
    "        \n",
    "    flush_nonweb()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nStep 2 Complete: {nonweb_total_docs:,} automated docs collected')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "--- \n",
    "## Step 3: Train / Val / Test Stratified Split Generation\n",
    "\n",
    "Streams all cleaned JSONL shards into 90% Train, 5% Val, and 5% Test files with zero RAM consumption and zero split leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "random.seed(42)\n",
    "out_txt = {s: open(f'{SPLITS_DIR}/{s}.txt', 'w', encoding='utf-8') for s in ['train', 'val', 'test']}\n",
    "out_json = {s: open(f'{SPLITS_DIR}/{s}.jsonl', 'w', encoding='utf-8') for s in ['train', 'val', 'test']}\n",
    "counts = {'train': 0, 'val': 0, 'test': 0}\n",
    "chars_per_split = {'train': 0, 'val': 0, 'test': 0}\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Partitioning shards into 90/5/5 train/val/test splits...')\n",
    "for d in [MANUAL_DIR, NONWEB_DIR, WEB_DIR]:\n",
    "    for sf in sorted(Path(d).glob('*.jsonl')):\n",
    "        with open(sf, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "            for line in f:\n",
    "                if not line.strip(): continue\n",
    "                r = random.random()\n",
    "                s = 'train' if r < 0.90 else ('val' if r < 0.95 else 'test')\n",
    "                out_json[s].write(line)\n",
    "                doc = json.loads(line)\n",
    "                t = doc.get('text', '')\n",
    "                if t.strip():\n",
    "                    out_txt[s].write(t.strip() + '\\n\\n')\n",
    "                counts[s] += 1\n",
    "                chars_per_split[s] += len(t)\n",
    "\n",
    "for f in out_txt.values(): f.close()\n",
    "for f in out_json.values(): f.close()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\n' + '=' * 60)\n",
    "print('SPLIT SUMMARY:')\n",
    "for s in ['train', 'val', 'test']:\n",
